  "body": "Currently, it is under-specified when new style sheets apply to the rendered output\r\nof a web page. In addition, the browsers have different heuristics and implementation\r\nstrategies for loading style sheets, especially during the load or parsing-HTML phase of\r\npage execution.\r\n\r\nIssue 1349 is the same as this, except for \"parsing behavior\".\r\ncrbug.com/481122 tracks rationalizing this in Chromium.\r\nblink-dev thread with lots of interesting data is here:\r\nhttps://groups.google.com/a/chromium.org/forum/#!searchin/blink-dev/css$20block/blink-dev/ZAPP8aTnyn0/JURBX5uFCAAJ\r\n\r\nThis was also recently discussed on public-web-perf:\r\nhttps://lists.w3.org/Archives/Public/public-web-perf/2018Jan/0021.html",
